{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Use Apache Curator's built-in namespace/chroot support for ZooKeeper tenant isolation; the namespace is exposed as a configuration property (e.g., xd.zookeeper.namespace in servers.yml) and all ZK paths in the codebase are made namespace-relative.",
    "U2: Implement HTTP Basic authentication on the Admin server REST endpoints; xd-shell prompts interactively for username/password on connect, holds credentials in memory only for the session, and never writes them to disk, shell history, or logs.",
    "U3: Adopt a maintenance-branch model (e.g., branch '1.0.x') with semantic versioning; MINOR/patch releases are cut from the maintenance branch and fixes are selectively merged back to master; CI jobs are configured for the new branch.",
    "U4: Remove deprecated module-registry functions (including download of module definitions) and their usages in Shell and Admin-UI; update or delete the corresponding tests; rely on the refactored registry API only.",
    "U5: Use ZooKeeper-based service discovery rather than a direct shell-to-ZK data connection: the Admin server publishes an ephemeral ZK node containing host and the actual (random) Tomcat port at startup; xd-shell resolves the Admin server endpoint from that node. This remains compatible with adding a load balancer later.",
    "U6: Migrate the Kafka message bus from the legacy consumer to the Kafka 0.9 new consumer API (org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer), adjusting offset management and configuration, then rerun and fix the previously failing tests.",
    "U7: Implement audio/video ingestion as a Motion-JPEG (multipart/x-mixed-replace) stream source module written in pure Java; the module parses the stream into JPEG frames and emits them as messages (byte[]) on the message bus; facial detection is performed by downstream analytics modules, so no native OpenCV dependency is introduced (per the platform-compatibility note).",
    "U8: Add a boolean configuration parameter (e.g., xd.ui.messageRates.enabled) in servers.yml; the value is exposed through an Admin endpoint and consumed by the Admin-UI cluster view to show or hide message rates.",
    "Baseline: the increment is built on the existing Spring XD codebase (Spring Framework with Java 17+ per the stated Spring 6 baseline), using Maven/Gradle builds, embedded ZooKeeper and embedded Kafka for integration tests."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All work is performed by a single developer (the author), so total effort equals the sum of individual activity efforts; no parallel work is assumed.",
    "An existing Spring XD codebase is available with ZooKeeper (Curator) integration, xd-shell, Admin server, message-bus abstraction, Kafka message bus module, and an Angular-based Admin-UI.",
    "Existing test infrastructure (embedded ZooKeeper, embedded Kafka, CI server) is available and functional.",
    "U7 is treated primarily as ingestion enablement: development of the facial-detection algorithm itself is out of scope; the spike is assumed to confirm Motion-JPEG feasibility.",
    "U3 involves SCM/CI and release-process setup only; no functional code changes are required beyond versioning configuration.",
    "For U6, a Kafka 0.9-compatible broker/cluster is available for testing, and the failing tests referenced are the known message-bus integration tests.",
    "Estimates include design, implementation, unit and integration testing, and activity-level documentation, but exclude elapsed-time delays such as environment outages or waiting on external reviews.",
    "No changes to the overall UI technology stack are needed for U8; only conditional rendering in the existing cluster view."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Design tenant-aware ZK namespace configuration",
      "activity_description": "Define the namespace configuration property, its semantics for tenant profiles, and how existing ZK paths become namespace-relative.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement ZK namespace support",
      "activity_description": "Wire the configurable namespace into the Curator client (namespace/chroot) and adapt path handling across components that read/write ZK metadata.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Namespace isolation tests",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests (embedded ZK) verifying metadata isolation between tenant namespaces and correct default behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Admin server authentication",
      "activity_description": "Add configurable Basic authentication to Admin server REST endpoints so credentials are supplied at runtime rather than stored in files.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Interactive shell credential prompt",
      "activity_description": "Implement interactive username/password prompt in xd-shell when targeting the Admin server; keep credentials in memory only for the session.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Security verification and tests",
      "activity_description": "Tests for authentication flows and verification that passwords are never persisted, echoed, or logged.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Maintenance branch setup",
      "activity_description": "Create the maintenance branch (e.g., 1.0.x), set the MINOR/patch versioning scheme, configure CI builds, and document the backport workflow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Remove deprecated module-definition download",
      "activity_description": "Delete deprecated module-registry functions (including download of module definitions) and migrate remaining callers to the refactored registry API.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Clean Shell and Admin-UI deprecated code",
      "activity_description": "Remove usages of deprecated functions from the Shell and Admin-UI modules and clean up dead code.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Regression fixes after cleanup",
      "activity_description": "Update/remove affected tests and fix regressions caused by the cleanup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spike: discovery approach evaluation",
      "activity_description": "Evaluate direct shell-to-ZK connection versus LB-mediated access versus ZK-based service discovery; document the decision.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Admin server endpoint registration",
      "activity_description": "Publish the Admin server host and actual random Tomcat port as an ephemeral ZooKeeper node at startup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Shell discovery and targeting",
      "activity_description": "Implement xd-shell lookup of the Admin server endpoint from ZK and a command to point the shell at the discovered server.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Discovery flow tests",
      "activity_description": "Integration tests covering startup registration, shell discovery, and reconnection behavior with random ports.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Upgrade to Kafka 0.9 new consumer API",
      "activity_description": "Migrate the Kafka message bus consumer code, configuration, and offset management to the Kafka 0.9 rewritten consumer.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Rerun and fix failing Kafka tests",
      "activity_description": "Rerun the previously failing message-bus tests against the new consumer and fix failures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Spike: Motion-JPEG feasibility and design",
      "activity_description": "Research Motion-JPEG ingestion feasibility and produce the design specification for the stream source module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Implement Motion-JPEG source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a pure-Java MJPEG (multipart/x-mixed-replace) stream source that parses the stream into individual JPEG frames.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Integrate frames with message bus and analytics hook",
      "activity_description": "Emit frames as messages on the message bus and provide the integration point for downstream predictive-analytics (facial detection) modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "U7 - MJPEG ingestion tests",
      "activity_description": "Tests with sample MJPEG streams validating frame extraction, message emission, and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Message-rates configuration parameter",
      "activity_description": "Add the enable/disable message-rates parameter to servers.yml and bind it into the Admin server configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Apply toggle in cluster view",
      "activity_description": "Expose the toggle via the Admin endpoint and update the Admin-UI cluster view to show/hide message rates accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Toggle tests",
      "activity_description": "Unit and UI-level tests for the enable/disable behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "Increment integration and system testing",
      "activity_description": "End-to-end testing of the combined increment across ZK, shell, Admin server, message bus, and Admin-UI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update configuration reference and user documentation for the new properties, shell behavior, and ingestion module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A26",
      "activity_name": "Build verification and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Final build verification, merge coordination with the maintenance branch, and release preparation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 43
  }
}
